    "narrative": "The Austin Waves head into today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** as our clear anchor, sporting a dominant 81.87 score against Brady Singer. While Singer isn't a league-worst arm, **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from an optimal lineup spot at #1 and a strong platoon advantage, making him our primary engine for R and RBI production. Complementing him is **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (72.72) and **Kyle Tucker** (71.61); **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** thrives against Mitch Keller due to a favorable 14% platoon boost and solid SP skill metrics, while **Kyle Tucker** remains an automatic start despite a mid-tier matchup against Michael King. **Heliot Ramos** also warrants attention; he carries a strong 69.02 score, buoyed significantly by a hitter-friendly park adjustment (+14%) and the opportunity to exploit Ryan Feltner.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Coby Mayo**, who finished with a 51.77 score. While **Coby Mayo** profiles well against Brady Singer, he was edged out by the superior defensive positioning and lineup volatility of our middle infield contingent. We are keeping a close watch on the rain risk affecting **Brayan Rocchio** and **Sam Antonacci** (both 38% risk); if these games see significant delays, their efficiency will plummet. Furthermore, while **Liam Hicks** and **Drake Baldwin** are penciled in to manage our catchers, their sub-60 scores remind us that we are relying more on floor stability than high-ceiling output at the C positions today. We remain cautious with **Jackson Merrill**, whose 53.23 score is suppressed by facing the elite arm of Shohei Ohtani, though his rostered role remains secure as we prioritize category-wide consistency.",
